      "artist": "Steve Morgan",
      "description": "Intel light rail shuttle bus southbound on Orenco Station Parkway just south of Cherry Drive, approaching Orenco MAX station. This New Flyer D40LF bus was operating on a regular shuttle service, for Intel employees only, which runs every day between the company's huge Ronler Acres campus and TriMet's Orenco/NW 231st MAX (light rail) station, in Hillsboro, Oregon. The service is operated by private charter-bus companies under contract. At the time of the photo, this bus was run by RAZ Transportation, a longtime charter operator in the Portland metropolitan area, while MTR Western was a second charter operator providing some shuttle service to Intel campuses in Hillsboro.  After RAZ went out of business in early 2014, its Intel service (and much of its bus fleet) were acquired by EcoShuttle, another charter-bus company.",
